  "finalText": "The 12-second password manager scene is built in the Main composition, in three beats of 4 seconds each, in a flat explainer style on a light mint background (#EAF4F4).\n\n- **Chaos (0–4 s):** seven coral and amber sticky notes pop in with a slight stagger, then jitter anxiously until 4 s. The jitter is an expression that fades out, so the notes are still when they start to move.\n- **Absorb (4–8 s):** each note arcs into a teal shield with a navy keyhole, shrinking as it goes. The shield pops in just as the first notes arrive, pulses once when the last one lands, and throws a soft amber glow.\n- **Resolve (8–12 s):** the headline \"One key. Every login.\" rises word by word from 8.2 s. A teal check badge draws its tick at about 9.1 s and holds through the end, so the frame settles at 12 s.\n\nThe check-mark badge sits above the headline rather than beside it, because beside it the badge overlapped the text. The layers are named (Note 1–7, Shield vault, Glow, Headline, Check badge) and the contact sheet shows the handoffs reading cleanly.\n\nI didn't add sound. Possible next tweaks: a bigger shield, a different palette, or a short caption under the headline."
